yet|PASS: The timetable question uses present-perfect yet and Vietnamese đã...chưa naturally; a polarity heuristic may flag it but there is no translation negation error. The separate conjunction joins small room with enough comfortable seats. Comma and register notes fit both distinct ordinals.
comply|PASS: Exhibitors complying with safety instructions illustrate comply with accurately. Vietnamese chấp hành/tuân thủ preserves obligation. Complied/compliance distinction is not conflated with a transitive comply something construction.
high|PASS: Wall height adjective, kite-position adverb and attendance-peak noun match three source ordinals. Vietnamese differentiates cao, lên cao and mức cao mới. The peak example specifies attendance and event; highly versus physical high is useful, without equating high with tall for every noun.
inflate|PASS: Tyre gas-filling matches the sole supplied boundary; bơm phồng retains action and before-valve-check timing. Active and intransitive grammar are accurate. Economic inflation is mentioned only as a contrast, not falsely sourced as an authored Sense.
prescribe|PASS: Qualified medical ordering and official model-size rule are distinct verb boundaries. Treatment example supplies no dose or medical recommendation. Vietnamese chỉ định and quy định are appropriate; transitive for complement and formal requirement register are accurate.
